  "camera_policy_choice": "adaptive, chosen by validation (0.412 vs 0.34 for full with the same weights). Late commands: the service applies about 44% of commands one frame late. lag=\"ahead\" (default) plans the next move from the pending command and sends it only if it is also legal from the current view. lag_replay.py, 8 held-out flights, 44% late: none 0.6245 (23 rejected), resend 0.6327 (0), ahead 0.6408 (0); no lag: 0.6225 for all. UPDATE: lag handling is back to none, Astra's original behaviour. Both none runs (0.412, 0.390) beat all four ahead/resend runs (0.36, 0.35, 0.334, 0.326). Part of that is network luck (none lost 1-2 frames, the others 11-21), but the recordings also show ahead taking only 9-13 level-2 views against 23-24 for none: planning from the pending camera position disrupts the zoom sequence that finds the small classes. Rejected moves cost only the move, which is cheaper than losing the zooms. DRONE_LAG selects none, resend or ahead."
